<title>CHINA: Shanghai uncovers largest car smuggling case.</title>
<headline>Shanghai uncovers largest car smuggling case.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai customs office has uncovered the largest smuggling case in the city's history involving 200 Japanese-made Honda cars worth 70 million yuan ($8.4 million), the Business News said on Friday.</p>
<p>An unnamed Chinese overseas commercial firm was found to have falsified commercial documents and had bought import licences to smuggle the cars into Shanghai, it said.</p>
<p>The cars are now being held by the customs and several suspects have admitted the smuggling attempt, the newspaper said. It gave no further details. ($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
